      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ugh, sorry for missing that this parameter ends up being unused here.\n\n\u003e BTW, should this function honor this bit and pass in `kRGB_888x_SkColorType` when it\u0027s set to true?\n\nThe `color_type` parameter of `EncodePNG` describes the format of the buffer pointed to by the `input` parameter.  So using `kRGB_888x_SkColorType` would be incorrect.\n\nI don\u0027t really know, but I am guessing that passing `kOpaque_SkAlphaType` (instead of `kUnpremul_SkAlphaType`) may work here.  Is this something you could try?  Or should I work on fixing this?\n\n\u003e I suspect it hasn\u0027t made a difference so far because when it\u0027s set to true, the input just happens to always have 255 as the alpha channel value.\n\nAck.",
      "parentUuid": "eff6439f_d1f70ccd",
      "revId": "2a2707c5e07b962995f3f89ef8da89fb95eac479",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
