      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Whoops. I saw \"888x\" and ran with it.\n\nIt\u0027s almost correct, but I think we would need `kBGR_888x_SkColorType` rather than `kRGB_888x_SkColorType` (to match `FPDFBitmap_BGRx` [used](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/pdfium/testing/helpers/write.cc;l\u003d208-210;drc\u003db2d540b15cad394746b9277911ae1192f25158aa) in `//third_party/pdfium/testing/helpers/write.cc` when `discard_transparency` is `true`).  And skia doesn\u0027t provide/define/support the `kBGR_888x_SkColorType` value.\n\n\u003e include/core/SkAlphaType.h says \"If SkAlphaType is kOpaque_SkAlphaType, and SkColorType is not opaque, then the result of drawing any pixel with a alpha value less than 1.0 is undefined.\" However, it looks like SkPngEncoderBase::getTargetInfo() and SkPngRustEncoderImpl::Make() handle kOpaque_SkAlphaType correctly. So could you give it a try?\n\nYes - let\u0027s continue the discussion in https://pdfium-review.googlesource.com/c/pdfium/+/138891 (after CQ passes)",
      "parentUuid": "20f812bc_9b616108",
